            {
                "entry_id": "e5fc8a5d-7fea-3e55-ba1e-b6c2adbeae82",
                "word": "Yu",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0a71d2a5-4af2-3a47-8da8-d4838feb8ebc",
                        "entry_id": "e5fc8a5d-7fea-3e55-ba1e-b6c2adbeae82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A county of Yangquan, Shanxi, China."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "caaa8855-3e38-45da-b249-da19add3977c",
                                "sense_id": "0a71d2a5-4af2-3a47-8da8-d4838feb8ebc",
                                "text": "She went to Yangquan Village of Yuxian County in Shanxi Province. Having never been to such a remote and backward countryside area with its scenic views and fresh air, Kang joked with her colleagues that it was like being on a tourist trip.",
                                "translation": "Face",
                                "english": "Face"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "973eb039-0c27-4d53-8195-1101269041b6",
                                "sense_id": "0a71d2a5-4af2-3a47-8da8-d4838feb8ebc",
                                "text": "Banners and a portrait of Communist Party Chairman Mao Zedong adorn the front of this strange-looking freight train making its first run in Yuxian County, Shanxi Province."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "11640d5a-57c5-3860-aebf-7d238ef4a314",
                "word": "yu",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "103bf167-7939-47c3-82ae-491edbfce07e",
                        "entry_id": "11640d5a-57c5-3860-aebf-7d238ef4a314",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "yu"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d30892f-095c-3845-ac61-f0784e7c5d52",
                        "entry_id": "11640d5a-57c5-3860-aebf-7d238ef4a314",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ancient Chinese wine-bucket, often having a decorative cover."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0eca548-37cd-4909-8310-952c48cf823e",
                                "sense_id": "4d30892f-095c-3845-ac61-f0784e7c5d52",
                                "text": "A group of slenderer yu also survive from the Shang into the early Chou period, though they are rarer than the other design […] A yu with square body in the Hakuzuru Museum is the finest of these."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e7ea087f-7cd4-38c1-9e61-173dc005d731",
                        "entry_id": "11640d5a-57c5-3860-aebf-7d238ef4a314",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Jade, nephrite or jadeite."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "09d3beb5-60cc-48d4-b6d5-38492f3c323d",
                                "sense_id": "e7ea087f-7cd4-38c1-9e61-173dc005d731",
                                "text": "The Yu, although of the hardness of rock crystal, is worked into an endless variety of forms […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "414f6d7d-e606-4442-bac5-5a29f2e148f2",
                                "sense_id": "e7ea087f-7cd4-38c1-9e61-173dc005d731",
                                "text": "Another stone with which it would be interesting to compare it is the celebrated yu stone of the Chinese, which Dr. Abel, in his work on China, conjectured to be a species of nephrite […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
